#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:33
msgid "Documents and format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:35
msgid "`--input` / `--report` / `-i`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:37
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Repeatable, and takes several values after one occurrence. Each value is "
"a **document specifier** in the `<url>:<path>:<name>` grammar — "
"{doc}`../../guides/user/documents` is that grammar in full, including how"
" a `:` inside a value is quoted and what `save_pdf` does in each case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:46
msgid ""
"Giving none from this source leaves the field **unset** rather than "
"empty, so a configuration file or the environment can still supply the "
"documents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:49
msgid "`--format` / `-f`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:51
msgid ""
"The format name, as `metadata/formats.csv` of the repository synthesises "
"it — `EURIZON-EN23`, `FINECO-EN23@LUX`, `MEDIOLANUM-IT24.A`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:54
msgid ""
"Omit it and the engine tries to infer it from the URL of each document, "
"using the repository's `url_mapping.csv`; the first matching prefix wins."
" Inference works only for documents that *have* a URL. Two documents "
"inferring **different** formats is an error rather than a choice made "
"silently. Giving `-f` explicitly while inference also succeeds and "
"disagrees is a warning, not an error: you were explicit, so you win, but "
"you are told."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:60
msgid "Where things live"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:62
msgid "`--formats-directory` / `--repo` / `-F` / `-r`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:64
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The formats repository. Note that the two tooling commands read a "
"**differently named** variable for the same thing — "
"`FREEPORTS_FORMATS_REPO`, not `FREEPORTS_FORMATS_REPO_PATH`; see "
"{doc}`index`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:68
msgid "`--db-directory` / `-I`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:70
msgid "The input database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:72
msgid "`--target-list` / `-T`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:74
msgid ""
"Repeatable, and takes several values after one occurrence. **This is the "
"check that runs first**: a configuration with no target list from any "
"source is rejected before a single PDF is opened."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:77
msgid ""
"From the environment the value is taken **whole** and never split, so a "
"list whose name contains a comma still works."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:80
msgid "Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:82
msgid "`--out` / `-o`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:84
msgid ""
"Where results go. A directory for `regular` and `structured`; a file for "
"`single_file` — and if the path does not end in `.csv` under that "
"profile, `out.csv` is appended to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:87
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The **parent** must exist; the directory itself need not. Defaults to the"
" working directory resolved to an absolute path, not to the literal `.` —"
" see {doc}`../configuration/options`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:90
msgid ""
"A path ending in `.tar.gz` switches the archive flag on and the suffix is"
" stripped, so `-o results.tar.gz` and `-o results -z` mean the same "
"thing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:93
msgid "`--out-profile` / `-P`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:95
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`regular` (default), `single_file`, or `structured`, case-insensitively. "
"{doc}`../../guides/user/output` says what each writes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:98
msgid "`--archive` / `-z` and `--separate-out`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:100
msgid ""
"Two independent flags: a compressed sibling of the output, and one CSV "
"per `(report, format)` pair for the two tables that carry them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:104
msgid ""
"Both flags can only be switched **on** from the command line. Present "
"means true; absent means *nothing said*, not false — otherwise every "
"command line would silently switch off what a configuration file had "
"turned on. To turn one off, say so where `false` can be written: "
"`FREEPORTS_ARCHIVE=false`, or `archive: false` in the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:112
msgid ""
"Sets `save_pdf` to false. Despite its name it does **not** suppress the "
"download — it suppresses *keeping* the downloaded file on disk. Absent "
"leaves the field unset; the default, from the defaults tier, is to keep."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:116
msgid "Batch and configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:118
msgid "`--batch` / `-b`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:120
#, python-brace-format
msgid "A CSV, one job per row. {doc}`../../guides/user/advanced/batch`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:124
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Use this configuration file instead of searching the three standard "
"tiers. {doc}`../configuration/config_file`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:127
msgid "Parallelism"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:129
msgid ""
"`--workers` / `-j` is the default for **both** levels; `--jobs` and "
"`--pages` override one each. Each takes a positive integer **or** the "
"word `auto`, and `auto` is a value you can write, not merely the absence "
"of one — it is how a level is put back to automatic after a configuration"
" file has pinned it to a number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:134
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Zero and negative values are a typed error naming the option you "
"mistyped, not a generic message about a concept. "
"{doc}`../../guides/user/advanced/parallelism`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:137
msgid "Verbosity: `-v` and `-q`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:138
msgid ""
"`-v` and `-q` are **counted** and are **independent dials**, not opposed "
"flags: the net of the two counts is added to the default and clamped, so "
"no combination is an error and `-vv -q` is legal."
msgstr ""

